tion.com/t/begin-the-rest-is-easy/263586","site":"T Nation · 2314 posts · 2019"},{"title":"(Un)Official 2024 T-ransformation Challenge","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/un-official-2024-t-ransformation-challenge/285956","site":"T Nation · 1288 posts · 2023"},{"title":"The Dating Thread","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-dating-thread/275759","site":"T Nation · 1209 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Ever Feel Like a Threadkiller? (16)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/ever-feel-like-a-threadkiller-16/149968","site":"T Nation · 1128 posts · 2010"},{"title":"NFL 2012/2013 Part 3","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/nfl-2012-2013-part-3/185998","site":"T Nation · 496 posts · 2013"},{"title":"More Crossfit Hating","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-crossfit-hating/172423","site":"T Nation · 306 posts · 2011"},{"title":"New Conan","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/new-conan/147426","site":"T Nation · 304 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Words/Phrases You Hate","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/words-phrases-you-hate/195675","site":"T Nation · 294 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Things You Hate About Yourself","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-you-hate-about-yourself/181707","site":"T Nation · 212 posts · 2012"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Bucket hat — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bucket_hat"},{"title":"Bucket hat - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bucket_hat"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Soft brimmed hat worn with an outfit","Changes head silhouette and frames the face","Adds a casual streetwear look and shade"],"effect":"direct","text":"Wearers use it as an accessory that sets the tone of an outfit and covers hair or scalp when they want."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bucket_hat","lead":["A bucket hat is a casual, brimmed hat made of soft fabric. It is said to date from around 1900, when Irish farmers and fishermen wore wool felt or tweed versions against rain; the natural lanolin in raw wool helped repel water [1].","The modern form descends from a lightweight olive-drab cotton hat issued to the US Army during the Vietnam War; civilians adopted it for fishing and sun protection [1]. Mods wore it in the 1960s, and rappers including LL Cool J and Run-DMC made it a hip-hop fashion item in the 1980s and 1990s [1].","It returned to catwalks in the 2010s after celebrities such as Rihanna wore it, and luxury houses including Gucci, Loewe and Prada have made versions [1]. As a style item it adds a streetwear or retro look and provides sun shade for the face."],"infobox":[["Type","Casual hat"],["Origin","Around 1900, Ireland (wool/tweed) [1]"],["Modern form","Cotton US Army hat, Vietnam War era [1]"],["Associated subcultures","Mod, hip-hop, football supporters (Argentina) [1]"],["Common uses","Streetwear, festivals, fishing, sun protection [1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["After the interwar years the Irish walking hat spread internationally because it folded into a coat pocket, could be sponged clean and could be reshaped with kettle steam [1]. The cotton military version later reached civilians, and in the 1960s Mod subculture members wore it and it was adapted into women's fashion [1].","In Argentina the hat is called the piluso and is tied to football supporter culture; its popularity there reportedly rose after the 2022 World Cup [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use for appearance","paras":["The bucket hat is typically worn for its casual look and for shade; Wikipedia lists festival wear, fishing and sun protection among its uses [1]. Online style discussion treats it as an easy way to add a retro or streetwear element."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"c. 1900","event":"Irish wool and tweed hats worn against rain [1]."},{"year":"1960s","event":"Adopted by Mod subculture and as women's fashion [1]."},{"year":"1980s-90s","event":"Rappers including LL Cool J and Run-DMC popularise it [1]."},{"year":"2010s","event":"Returns to catwalks; luxury brands produce versions [1]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Bucket hat","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bucket_hat","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Bucket hat","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bucket_hat","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Anna's Training Log Part 2 (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/annas-training-log-part-2-part-1/258235","site":"T Nation · 9999 posts · 2019"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8675 posts · 2021"},{"title":"The Push to 2020 Has Begun!","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-push-to-2020-has-begun/257948","site":"T Nation · 5555 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Boilerman Wants It All","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/boilerman-wants-it-all/254882","site":"T Nation · 4422 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Davemccright's Dangerous Dave’s Diabolical Log for Density and Destruction","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/davemccrights-dangerous-dave-s-diabolical-log-for-density-and-destruction/273294","site":"T Nation · 2615 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Wisey's Training Log - StrongEveryDay","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/wiseys-training-log-strongeveryday/276826","site":"T Nation · 2457 posts · 2022"}]}